---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Gallery from '../Gallery.astro';

// Original Assets
import imgBeacon from '../../assets/Introduction/BLE Beacon Top Down.jpg';
import imgViper  from '../../assets/Introduction/Viper Link Top Down.jpg';
import imgWasp   from '../../assets/Introduction/wasp-with-tr-edited.jpg';

// Research Application Montage Assets
import imgEgg       from '../../assets/Introduction/dummy-egg.jpg';
import imgFrog      from '../../assets/Introduction/frog-w-transmitter-clean.jpg';
import imgBat       from '../../assets/Introduction/jeladó denevéren.jpg';
import imgButterfly from '../../assets/Introduction/lepke jeladó papilio antimachus.jpg';
import imgMouse     from '../../assets/Introduction/mouse-implant.jpg';
import imgOwl       from '../../assets/Introduction/owl-w-transmitter.jpg';
import imgVole      from '../../assets/Introduction/root-vole-clean.jpg';
import imgHedgehog  from '../../assets/Introduction/suni.jpg';
import imgTit       from '../../assets/Introduction/széncinege jeladó.jpg';
import imgViperImpl     from '../../assets/Introduction/rákosi vipera beültetett jeladó.jpg';
---

<section class="intro-section" id="introduction">
  <div class="page-container">

    <div class="intro-text reveal">
      <h1 class="section-title">Introduction</h1>
      <p class="body-text">
        Our Bluetooth-based radio telemetry system supports a wide variety of wildlife research goals.
        Most importantly, it allows for long-term, continuous monitoring of individual animals,
        potentially over their entire lifespan. By using multiple receivers, you can track animal
        activity and estimate their positions using radio fingerprinting. The transmitters can also
        be equipped with different sensors, such as temperature sensors.
      </p>
      <p class="body-text" style="margin-top:1rem;">
        The system uses a custom version of the Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) protocol to improve battery
        life and transmission range. The transmitters come in many sizes, from an ultra-lightweight
        60&nbsp;mg tag to larger units weighing a few grams that can operate for over 5 years.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="intro-gallery-wrap reveal" style="transition-delay:0.15s;">
      <Gallery
        containerId="intro-gallery"
        images={[
          { src: imgBeacon, alt: "BLE beacon top-down view", caption: "BLE Beacon Top-Down View" },
          { src: imgWasp, alt: "Hornet (Vespa crabro) with radio transmitter attached", caption: "Hornet (Vespa crabro) with a Transmitter" },
          { src: imgViper, alt: "BLE receiver top-down view", caption: "BLE Receiver Top-Down View" },
        ]}
        autoSlideInterval={5000}
      />
    </div>

    <div class="apps-intro reveal" style="transition-delay:0.1s;">
      <p class="body-text">
        The table below highlights various potential use cases and research applications supported by the system:
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="apps-split-grid">
      
      <div class="apps-table-card glass-card reveal">
        <table class="apps-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Research Application</th>
              <th>Description</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Insect Tracking</strong></td>
              <td>Deploying ultra-lightweight transmitters (down to 60 mg) to study the movement patterns and behaviors of small insect species.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Urban Wildlife Monitoring</strong></td>
              <td>Tracking the behavior, home ranges, and habitat utilization of urban wildlife, such as hedgehogs, within developed environments.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Bat Monitoring</strong></td>
              <td>Monitoring bats to analyze fine-scale local movements, foraging flight activity, and roosting habits.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Small Mammal Tracking</strong></td>
              <td>Studying tunnel, runway, and burrow usage among small mammals to map underground or covered activity patterns.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Avian Nest Box Studies</strong></td>
              <td>Monitoring songbirds to log individual nest box visits. Unlike RFID systems that only record actual entry, BLE can detect proximity. This shows when a bird simply checks a nest from a nearby branch and flies away.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Reptile Body Temperature</strong></td>
              <td>Tracking reptiles while continuously logging real-time changes in their body temperature.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Microclimate & Environmental Monitoring</strong></td>
              <td>Logging localized environmental parameters, including ambient temperature, humidity, and soil moisture alongside animal telemetry data.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Incubation & Breeding Studies</strong></td>
              <td>Utilizing sensor-equipped dummy eggs to gather precise temperature, orientation, and handling data during avian nesting cycles.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Multi-Year Monitoring</strong></td>
              <td>Conducting continuous, multi-year, or lifelong behavioral studies on small home-range species.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="apps-montage-container reveal" style="transition-delay:0.15s;">
        <div class="photo-pile">
          
          <div class="pile-card img-bat" style="z-index: 10;">
            <Image src={imgBat} alt="Radio transmitter on a bat" class="zoomable" />
          </div>
          

          <div class="pile-card img-egg" style="z-index: 11;">
            <Image src={imgEgg} alt="Tracking sensors embedded inside a dummy egg" class="zoomable" />
          </div>

          <div class="pile-card img-owl" style="z-index: 12;">
            <Image src={imgOwl} alt="Owl equipped with a transmitter unit" class="zoomable" />
          </div>
          
          <div class="pile-card img-mouse" style="z-index: 13;">
            <Image src={imgMouse} alt="Small mammal tracking implant view" class="zoomable" />
          </div>
          
          <div class="pile-card img-frog" style="z-index: 14;">
            <Image src={imgFrog} alt="Miniature transmitter attached safely to a frog" class="zoomable" />
          </div>
          
          <div class="pile-card img-butterfly" style="z-index: 15;">
            <Image src={imgButterfly} alt="Papilio antimachus butterfly tracking experiment" class="zoomable" />
          </div>
          
          <div class="pile-card img-vole" style="z-index: 16;">
            <Image src={imgVole} alt="Root vole telemetry movement profiling" class="zoomable" />
          </div>
          
          <div class="pile-card img-tit" style="z-index: 17;">
            <Image src={imgTit} alt="Great tit bird with proximity logging unit" class="zoomable" />
          </div>
          
          <div class="pile-card img-hedgehog" style="z-index: 18;">
            <Image src={imgHedgehog} alt="Hedgehog tag attachment overview" class="zoomable" />
          </div>

          <div class="pile-card img-viper" style="z-index: 19;">
            <Image src={imgViperImpl} alt="Viper implant transmitter overview" class="zoomable" />
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<style>
.intro-section {
  padding-block: 5rem 4rem;
}

.intro-text {
  margin-bottom: 2rem;
}

.intro-gallery-wrap {
  margin-top: 2rem;
}

.apps-intro {
  margin-top: 4.5rem;
  margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
}

/* Split Column Configuration */
.apps-split-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1.25fr 1fr;
  gap: 3.5rem;
  align-items: center;
}

/* ── Application Specifications Table ──────────────────────── */
.apps-table-card {
  overflow: hidden;
  border: 1px solid rgba(78, 204, 163, 0.12);
}

.apps-table {
  width: 100%;
  border-collapse: collapse;
}

.apps-table thead tr {
  background: rgba(78, 204, 163, 0.14);
  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(78, 204, 163, 0.2);
}

.apps-table th {
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  font-size: 0.68rem;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.16em;
  color: var(--c-teal);
  padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
  text-align: left;
  font-weight: 700;
}

.apps-table td {
  padding: 0.85rem 1.1rem;
  font-size: 0.86rem;
  line-height: 1.5;
  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(78, 204, 163, 0.07);
  vertical-align: top;
  color: var(--c-text-dim);
}

.apps-table td strong {
  color: #ffffff;
  font-weight: 600;
}

.apps-table tr:nth-child(even) td {
  background: rgba(22, 40, 36, 0.25);
}

.apps-table tr:last-child td {
  border-bottom: none;
}

/* ── Fluid Aspect-Ratio Photo Montage Pile ─────────────────── */
.apps-montage-container {
  width: 100%;
}

.photo-pile {
  position: relative;
  width: 100%;
  aspect-ratio: 1 / 1; /* Locks layout proportions down across all dimensions */
  margin-inline: auto;
  margin-top: 1rem;
}

/* Single Frame Base Graphic Architecture */
.pile-card {
  position: absolute;
  border-radius: 0.35rem;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 
    0 10px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5),
    0 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
  background: #0d1211;
  transition: 
    transform 0.35s cubic-bezier(0.25, 1, 0.5, 1), 
    box-shadow 0.3s ease, 
    z-index 0s;
}

.pile-card :global(.zoomable) {
  width: 100%;
  height: auto;
  display: block;
}

.pile-card:hover {
  transform: scale(1.1) rotate(0deg) !important;
  box-shadow: 
    0 25px 50px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7), 
    0 0 15px rgba(78, 204, 163, 0.25);
  z-index: 99 !important;
}

/* Absolute Layout Matrix Coordinates (Driven by Source Aspect Ratios) */
.img-bat {
  width: 38%;
  top: 2%;
  left: 2%;
  transform: rotate(-6deg);
}

.img-owl {
  width: 25%;
  top: 0%;
  right: 13%;
  transform: rotate(5deg);
}

.img-egg {
  width: 36%;
  top: -15%;
  left: 36%;
  transform: rotate(3deg);
}

.img-frog {
  width: 41%;
  top: 36%;
  left: 4%;
  transform: rotate(8deg);
}

.img-mouse {
  width: 38%;
  top: 27%;
  left: 35%;
  transform: rotate(-3deg);
}

.img-butterfly {
  width: 36%;
  top: 33%;
  right: 2%;
  transform: rotate(-5deg);
}

.img-vole {
  width: 36%;
  bottom: 9%;
  left: 7%;
  transform: rotate(-4deg);
}

.img-hedgehog {
  width: 36%;
  bottom: -10%;
  left: 60%;
  transform: rotate(-5deg);
}

.img-tit {
  width: 40%;
  bottom: 16%;
  right: 12%;
  transform: rotate(9deg);
}

.img-viper {
  width: 26%;
  bottom: -19%;
  left: 38%;
  transform: rotate(4deg);
}


/* ── Responsive Display Adaptations ───────────────────────── */
@media (max-width: 1024px) {
  .apps-split-grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 4rem;
  }
  
  .photo-pile {
    max-width: 480px; /* Clamps layout scale maximum constraint on mid screens */
  }
}

@media (max-width: 600px) {
  .apps-intro {
    margin-top: 3.5rem;
  }
  
  .apps-table th, 
  .apps-table td {
    padding: 0.7rem 0.85rem;
  }
  
  .apps-table th {
    font-size: 0.62rem;
  }
  
  .apps-table td {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }
}
</style>